; What lz adds to the root's env. A stanza names no flag of its own, except a
; unit compiled for an instruction set extension.
;
; Every profile but sanitize compiles the C at -O3, so that the benches and
; tests run the code a release build ships. The sanitize profile keeps
; :standard's level: it runs tests, never benches, and less inlining keeps
; its reports' stack traces closer to the source.
;
; Under sanitize lz's executables also link the debug runtime and stress the
; collector as rig's do (packages/rig/dune), so that a value a stub holds
; unrooted fails at once. The decoders parse untrusted bytes, and these runs are the proof
; that no kernel reads or writes outside its buffers.

(env
 (sanitize
  (link_flags
   (:standard -runtime-variant d))
  (env-vars
   (OCAMLRUNPARAM s=4k,o=20,M=1,m=1,V=1)))
 (_
  (c_flags
   (:standard -O3))))
